  "releaseNotes": "v5.2.0: Catch-all routes. A route or rewrite pattern ending in {*name} (for example /api/{*rest}) matches zero or more remaining path segments and captures the raw remainder. Routes without a catch-all always take precedence; among catch-alls the most specific wins (longest literal prefix). Invalid patterns are rejected by the management API with 400, flagged by /config/validate, skipped with a warning on import, and never match. New public RouteMatcher class. Watson 7.2.1 (UrlMatcher 3.1.0).",
